  "text": {
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lily's class has a garden. It is next to the classroom. There is a sign on the wall. It says: \"Our class garden.\" Teacher Kim and the children go in. \"This is our garden,\" says Teacher Kim. The flowers are red, pink, and yellow. Mia says, \"I like that red flower.\"",
      "Leo runs to the flowers. \"Look at that sign, Leo,\" says May. The sign says: \"Don't run.\" Leo stops. \"Sorry, May,\" he says. \"Where is the garden of Class One?\" asks Lily. It is behind the classroom. The children go there. A sign there says: \"Class One garden.\" \"Their flowers are white,\" says Mia.",
      "Teacher Kim shows a new sign. \"What does this sign say?\" she asks. Lily reads, \"Close the door, please.\" \"Yes!\" says Teacher Kim. May closes the door. \"Signs are good,\" says Teacher Kim. \"They say what to do.\" The children smile. It is a very nice garden."
    ],
    "summary": "Lily's class has a garden next to the classroom. The children read four signs and learn what to do.",
